Z||000000||Fearless Freep||10-06-2000||05:25 PM||||Cruising home tonight and up in the distance I spot a stalled car....I was not planning to stop, when I noticed that it was an 85 Gold SE.....Naturally now it became a moral obligation  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>He said that he was just driving along and all of a sudden the RPMS shot up and the car would no longer move forward. (I figured a blown hose?? Help me out)<P>Anyways I ask him to pop the trunk to look at his engine and I had to friggin squeegee the oil off the engine to even see anything.  He calmly replied that he had a small oil leak somewhere....NO KIDDING!! Anyways, the car would run, just not move forward.  I could tell the o2 sensor was toasted/cracked, most of the hoses were worn and getting crusty. <P>Long story short......I gave him a ride to the next exit gas station.  Just for my information (in case Im in this situation again,) what would have been some good key points to have checked?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula||10-06-2000||05:44 PM||||transmission coolant lines ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||10-06-2000||06:41 PM||||Or no tranny fluid at all anymore (happened to me once when a hose cracked).||||reg||1
